endobj
6668 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 22460 0 R
/E (In object-oriented programming \(OOP\), inheritance is a process of one class \(derived class\) inheriting properties and behaviors of an existing class \(base class\). This enhances the concept of reusing code through the inheritance of the shared attributes and functions in derived classes instead of copying them. The derived class can then inherit or alter the inherited characteristics giving rise to a specialized version of the base class.)
/Pg 90 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
