<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 22781 0 R
/E (Encapsulation in OOP is the process of bundling data \(attributes\) and the methods \(functions\) that operate on that data into a single unit, typically a class. It involves hiding the internal state of an object and controlling access to it through public methods \(like getters and setters\), thereby protecting the data from unauthorized modification and ensuring data integrity. )
/Pg 102 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
